module_doc "The nodes of the parsed tree that no other dump of it holds: `provides`, the\nmarks of a parameter and of a function type, the handlers of a failing call,\n`yield`, `try`, `assert`, `defer`, `undo`, `fail`, `dispatch`, `parallel`,\n`sync` on two objects, `select`, a walk by pointer, `here`, an anonymous\nfunction with a result, a pattern and `delete` and `destroy` with an\nallocator. The parser takes the file and the checker would refuse it, so\n`--dump-ast` is its one use."
